            <p>A cruise to Italy combines the best of art, history, food, and coastline beauty all into one trip. While your boat is still in the water, the closer you get to Italy, the more you will see the coastline lined with old buildings. As the boat approaches the pastel colored towns of Italy, an ancient feeling will come over you. You will see endless and ancient architecture as you approach the city. You will see the architectural borders of the old Mediterranean. It is a feeling that Italy has evoked in countless people at the fringes of Italy’s borders. Italy’s cities and ports are the intertwined lifeblood of a multi-generational culture. </p>

            <p>There is a journey taken on the sea that is unmatchable by taking a flight. You get to enter ancient ports still untouched by modern-day civilisation. Instead of taking separated and congested highways, your boat is unblocked and free to move as it pleases. Cruises to Italy allow the traveller to go to multiple famous places. </p>

            <h2>Cruise to the Adriatic and Venice, Italy</h2>

            <p>Venice, Italy cruises offer one of the most restorative experiences of the Mediterranean. The regal buildings and exquisite bridges in Venice will surpass all of your expectations. As you enter the city on a cruise, it will add to the luxurious feeling as you enter the floating city of Venice. </p>

            <p>Adriatic itineraries outside Venice typically include ports on Italy's eastern coastline, as well as nearby countries. Travellers can enjoy seaside villages, ancient cathedrals, regional cuisine, and more. Of all cruises to Venice, Italy, the best is the one that offers both adventure and sophistication. </p>

            <h2>MSC Rome and Italian Departures</h2>

            <p>All Rome itineraries with <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/msc-cruise-line">MSC Cruises</a> start at the port of Civitavecchia, which is the gateway to the Italian capital. When you have Rome as your starting point, with the Colosseum and the Vatican, you already have some of the most important history of the whole Mediterranean, and then you can head off on a cruise. MSC offers the most up-to-date ships, and with them, the best of modern Europe with all its style. </p>
            <p>Typically, MSCC has cruises that include Rome, along with Naples, and nearby ports in Sicily and Florence. This combination of historical and cultural landmarks, along with spectacular Mediterranean beaches and coastlines, makes for a more diverse cruise itinerary. Onboard, passengers enjoy the best of Italian hospitality, and on land, they enjoy Italy's cultural treasures. </p>

            <h2>Princess Italy and Mediterranean Elegance</h2>

            <p>Each of the Italy cruises with <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/princess-cruises">Princess Cruises</a> offers a unique combination of comfort and one-of-a-kind experiences on shore. This is true for all cruises that operate in the Mediterranean and include ports in Italy, including Rome, Naples, and Venice, which is also known to have classical beauty and charm, and offers excellent service. This cruise line offers a wide variety of activities designed with a focus on local and regional culture, and is known for its exceptional attention to detail and customer service. </p>
            <p>Depending on the day, guests on a Princess Italy cruise may take a high-class dinner after visiting ancient ruins. This is a natural transition from historic street life to modern elegance on board. It is the Art, architecture and cuisine of Italy that set the tempo of the cruise for the day. </p>

            <h2>Cruise Lines Sailing to Italy</h2>

            <p>Most of the cruise lines on your list offer Italy as a regular feature on their European itineraries. MSC Cruises, Princess Cruises, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/royal-caribbean-cruises">Royal Caribbean</a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/celebrity-cruise-line">Celebrity Cruises</a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/norwegian-cruise-line">Norwegian Cruise Line</a>, <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/costa-cruise-line">Costa Cruises</a> and <a href="https://www.fareschoices.com/holland-america-cruises">Holland America Line</a> have Mediterranean sailings with ports in Italy. Cunard Line, P&O Cruises, and Oceania Cruises also have specific itineraries that include Italy. </p>

            <p>Destination-based itineraries are utilized by the newer cruise lines Viking Ocean Cruises (along with Windstar), as well as the luxury lines of Regent Seven Seas, Seabourn Cruise Line, Silversea Cruises, and Ponant. Each cruise line has a distinct personality, but all provide access to Italy’s exceptional cities and stunning coastlines. </p>
            <h2>Italy's Cruising Plus Travel Beyond the Ports</h2>

            <p>Italy is sailed by cruise ships that offer excursions, allowing cruise travelers discover different regions. Starting with the North, their first stop is Venice and its ancient Renaissance buildings. Next is the central region, Rome, with ancient ruins and a lively fusion of modern culture. Finally, in the South, with views of Mt. Vesuvius and the ancient ruins of Pompeii, they stop in Naples.In all regions, Italian cuisine is offered. Italy is famous for its exquisite pasta, seafood and olive oil, and for their local wines. Because of the endless history that Italy has, unique dining experiences are created. </p>

            <h2>Cruise Life Italy</h2>

            <p>While Italy is the cruise destination, the onboard cruise life is lively yet sophisticated. During Mediterranean sailings, the entertainment is sophisticated cuisine, culture, and themed nights. Guests sit together and enjoy the coast while the decks are warm with a sea breeze. Sophisticated dinners are served, and the onboard culture is lively. Excursions during the cruise are of a different culture and provide an oasis on board. </p>

            <h2>Booking with Fareschoices</h2>

            <p>While planning a cruise to Italy, one does not only need to pinpoint the departure ports and cruise lines, and even the travel dates, but also consider several other factors. This is certainly an added burden for many, but for some, the research is justified. Options include MSC Rome sailings, Princess Italy voyages, and cruises in between. </p>

            <p> Fareschoices simplifies the selection process and is the most efficient way to do so. You can here check itineraries and compare MSC Cruises, Princess Cruises, Royal Caribbean,  Celebrity Cruises, Norwegian Cruise Line and other cruise lines. This will let you easily and without doubt get the cruise you wanted. </p>

            <h2>How to create memories that last</h2>

            <p>Italy’s beauty from the water is astonishing. Coastal cliffs and harbours are dramatic views, but the addition of colourful villages makes it even more so. Each little village makes the approach to each new port exciting. </p>

            <p>No travel experience captures the spirit of the Mediterranean like a cruise to Italy. It combines all the elements of the journey: art, food, architecture, and the varying natural landscapes of each region. Whether it is strolling the ancient streets of Rome or sailing towards Venice at sunset, it is an experience one holds onto forever. </p>

            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

            <h3>1. What is the best time of year to cruise to Italy? </h3>

            <p>Most Mediterranean cruises operate during late spring to early fall when the weather is most pleasant, and the ports are fully open. </p>

            <h3>2. Do cruises to Venice still operate? </h3>

            <p>Yes, a number of cruise lines are still able to schedule Venice and nearby cruise ports based on current ship regulations and sailing itineraries. </p>

            <h3>3. MSC Cruises Rome Departure Port? </h3>

            <p>Civitavecchia is the main cruise ship port for Rome and is the default port of all calls. </p>

            <h3>4. First-time cruiser: Is Princess Italy right for me? </h3>

            <p>Yes, Princess Italy sailings are very suitable for first-time travellers, as they include a good mix of experiences and excursions on the shore. </p>

            <h3>5. What is the easiest way to book a cruise? </h3>

